# Build context hygiene (M18; workspace layout since the monorepo split).
#
# The two entries that matter for correctness are `.env*` — a secret must reach
# the container through the platform, never through a layer — and `node_modules`,
# which would otherwise shadow the stage's own `pnpm install` with the host's
# (glibc) binaries inside an Alpine image.
#
# **Every pattern here is anchored unless it starts with `**/`.** Docker's
# ignore syntax is not gitignore's: a bare `node_modules` matches only the one
# at the context root, so a nested `apps/*/node_modules` — or, far worse, a
# nested `.env` — would be copied straight into the image. Anything that can
# legitimately appear at more than one depth is written `**/…`.

.git
.github
.husky
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.next-e2e-google
**/out
**/build
**/coverage

# secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
!apps/web/.env.example

# test artefacts
**/e2e/.auth
**/e2e/test-results
**/e2e/playwright-report
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# local tooling
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.worktrees
**/docker-compose.yml
**/docker-compose.test.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
